# mutgap_tex_readonly_heap_write: In the service a read-only heap (flag bit 2; argument buffers are on) is a detach heap made with the private resource option 0x1000000, and so is its cover buffer, which is what the heap is as a blit buffer. A fill of the heap as a buffer, and a fill of a buffer placed in it, both complete and leave its guest pages as they were (the GPU drops the writes, as for a read-only buffer, resources_readonly_buffer); a fill of a shared heap lands. Isolate only: in-process a read-only heap is refused (resources_heap_setups_inproc).
